{
  "id": "COMPOUND:17951 - PROTEIN:1106",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which o-Orsellinaldehyde interacts with the Gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit gamma-2, through a series of target interactions involving the Epidermal growth factor receptor. This pathway is supported by multiple high-scoring connections, with o-Orsellinaldehyde acting as a target for several compounds that ultimately target the gamma-2 subunit. The shared involvement of the Epidermal growth factor receptor in all three paths indicates a common mechanism of action, possibly through the modulation of receptor signaling pathways. The presence of multiple compounds with similar target profiles further strengthens the hypothesis that o-Orsellinaldehyde may exert its effects by influencing the same receptor or downstream signaling events. The integrated evidence points to a plausible, mechanistically grounded relationship, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
